{"kind":"assert","text":"J4 later phases: I release rehold to you, and only that command. This act also says what the token channel needs.\n\n## Finisher\n\nThe finisher exited 0. `commands.after-admission.json` is sha256 62c7af877b9786faef8c9c74855a6ec11aa63b8ba744795f029bb4fb74b80de0, and `finisher-readback.json` is 4b3349ce0f77967dc656dbd49b75d4c2f41901e6721c33899cd3df5f39583fc1. The sealed copy is `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-31-j4-later-packet-v16-finish`, `SHA256SUMS` db3eac70d627f31541754e1e48fa6338988e6df638e2798b6d9e0757dc81b6b3. Every later phase is held ready: `j4-release.py` in that unit checks the previous phase's receipt and public result, then fills the parent digest.\n\n## Before rehold\n\nCheck these four things. A failure here spends nothing, so tell me and I will change the input.\n\n1. `shasum -a 256 /private/tmp/artroom-j4-provider-channel-packet-20261030-v4/packet-binding.json` gives b054c7dbe47b2019dca935b9ba88583b5530ec4bf89f8b20de03c7b55723b1a7.\n2. Your Cloudflare custody still works: `npx -y wrangler@4.147.0 whoami`, from a scratch directory.\n3. Nothing listens on port 18787, the port in the channel input.\n4. `~/.config/generalbusiness/j4-staging-2026-10-30b/provider-channel-v4-1` has no `HALTED.json`, `selected-info` or `mint-read`.\n\n## Rehold\n\nRun it in a shell with no `NODE_OPTIONS`, no `NODE_DEBUG` and no preload. Index 52 is the parent 292e26368b4171a7f58b8173f76c1b7ed71d9071e551aebbbbc640652ab05a4d.\n\n```\npython3 /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-operator-packet-20261031-v16/collector.py --source-root /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom/.builder-worktrees/j4-landed-source-20261031-v1 --packet-dir /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-operator-packet-20261031-v16 --capture-root /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-acceptance-evidence-20261031-v16 --private-vault /Users/hughpyle/.config/generalbusiness/j4-live-2026-10-30/vault-v6 --packet-sha256 19b4eb1edfa29e1a20e6f2220f031c185d852b0cfbfefd20b7d647e39110636a --checkpoint 112eff124e7a51d2ebdd2d100ae24b52d03848ac --tree 32947a56902395b3f86eec91055fc6be3dfb7d84 --label hosted-j4-later-v16-1-rehold --timeout 240 -- node --import /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom/.builder-worktrees/j4-landed-source-20261031-v1/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-operator-packet-20261031-v16/operator.mjs --phase rehold --input /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-public-input-reviewed-20261030-v1/input.reviewed.json --source-root /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom/.builder-worktrees/j4-landed-source-20261031-v1 --vault /Users/hughpyle/.config/generalbusiness/j4-live-2026-10-30/vault-v6 --public /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-acceptance-evidence-20261031-v16/public-later-v16-1-rehold --label later-v16-1-rehold --packet-binding /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-operator-packet-20261031-v16/packet-binding.json --packet-sha256 19b4eb1edfa29e1a20e6f2220f031c185d852b0cfbfefd20b7d647e39110636a --capture-root /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-acceptance-evidence-20261031-v16 --private-binding /Users/hughpyle/.config/generalbusiness/j4-live-2026-10-30/private-binding.json --continuation-sha256 2f4ebadf1d21b9a4939f1d3b3a813d20158ada7a060cee556dd7f95b1b9386ee --predecessor-input /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-acceptance-evidence-20261031-v15/public-setup-v15-1/result.json --predecessor-sha256 c99c942df079dc1c52eb834d7090b21f579bade47a002347460530dfe077f9b1 --parent-state-sha256 292e26368b4171a7f58b8173f76c1b7ed71d9071e551aebbbbc640652ab05a4d\n```\n\nStop on any classification other than `rehold-complete`. That includes `rehold-complete-leftovers-open`, which exits 0.\n\n## The token channel, in order\n\n1. You run rehold and tell me the result. I write the `selected-info` input from `forks.a` and `holds.a` in its public result, and I send you the exact command with the input's SHA.\n2. You run `selected-info`. It took 8 s in the dry run, and the outer deadline is 180 s. This call starts no token clock. Tell me when it finishes.\n3. I send one act with the `mint-read` input, which binds the selected-info receipt by path and SHA, and with the `work` command, parent digest filled. That act releases `work` on the condition in step 5, so your 585 s does not wait on my turn. If you want a separate release after the mint, say so now.\n4. You run `mint-read`, with `--vault` the same `provider-channel-v4-1`.\n5. You copy the token file to the operator's fixed path, then read `channel-result.json` in the mint-read capture. It must show `outcome` `minted-read-credential`, `commandExit` 0, `processClosed` true, and an `ends` about 900 s away. Then run `work`, with `ends` more than 315 s away when `work` starts.\n\n## Three facts the commands depend on\n\n- **Two vaults.** `channel.py:125` refuses any vault outside `j4-staging-2026-10-30b`, so the channel cannot write into `vault-v6`. The operator reads `vault-v6/mint-read/independent-read.json`. Create `vault-v6/mint-read` with mode 0700 and copy the file there with mode 0600, because `safety.mjs:23` refuses any other mode. Do not use a link, because `safety.mjs:16` refuses one. Keep the channel's copy: `revoke-read` requires that exact path (`credential_binding.py:71`).\n- **Capture names.** `outer_capture.py:53` requires the prefix `artroom-j4-provider-channel-outer-20261030-v4-`. The commands I send use `-selected-info-1` and `-mint-read-1`, and neither exists now. Leave the provenance file where the channel writes it, beside `channel-result.json`, because the token file names that path and its SHA.\n- **Fork ID.** The channel requires the fork's `id` and `name` to equal the repository name, and rehold's fork rows have that form. The provider's own `info.id` differs (`69zzk7jzn3hndooa` in the dry run). The channel does not compare it.\n\n## What I checked, and what nobody has run\n\nI compared the channel's output with `parseIndependent` by reading both: file keys, provenance keys, `repository` as host `artifacts`, namespace `dap-demo` and name as ID, `reviewBasis`, and `runLabel`. They match. The rehearsal wrote this form with its own code (`rehearse-later.mjs:433`), so no file from the real channel has met the operator. I ran my input helper once on V15's public result, and it passed the channel's input checks as I copied them. It did not run the channel.\n\nIf the file fails, `work` stops with `work-independent-read-*` before its first original. A failed `selected-info` or `mint-read` writes `HALTED.json`, and an interrupted mint stays unknown. Neither allows a retry or a new mint. Each comes back to you and me.\n\nThe finding-views gate runs on this machine from 18:13 EDT, so expect slower local work until it ends. Rehold's limit is 240 s.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0894c80ea95ff33ccbf769b8b82bee2626768518, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2325d2bdec8bb369d6c3cd77d8163d178ccacc09 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more"}}